# data/ — reads only

One file per entity: `data/projects.ts`, `data/users.ts`.

- Every SELECT lives here — never `.from(...).select()` in a page or component
- Prefer importing the server client; pass a client in only when the caller must choose browser vs server
- Select only needed columns — never `select('*')`
- Throw on Supabase `error`; return `data`. Use `ts-pattern` when branching on result/error unions instead of long `if`/`switch` chains

```ts
export async function getProjectsByUser(userId: string) {
  const supabase = await createClient()
  const { data, error } = await supabase
    .from('projects')
    .select('id, name, status')
    .eq('user_id', userId)
  if (error) throw error
  return data
}
```
